closeout/prepare.go:273:\tplan.ExtraLogPaths = extraPaths\ninternal/reaper/finish.go:167:\t// ExtraLogs are further host logs to commit beside the handle's log: the\ninternal/reaper/finish.go:169:\tExtraLogs []string\ninternal/reaper/finish.go:252:\tcj.Worker, cj.ExtraLogs, cj.Review = o.Worker, o.ExtraLogs, o.Review\ninternal/worker/run.go:866:\tout, err := d.Finisher.FinishWith(ctx, jb.sj.ID, s.h, s.st, res, reaper.FinishOptions{Cause: cause, Worker: w, ExtraLogs: extra})\n// Package roles holds the starter .ard/ tree that `ard init` (#27) proposes\n// to a target repo. Paths in FS are relative to .ard/ (for example\n// \"config.yaml\" or \"scanners/cve/scan\"). embed.FS reports every file as 0444,\n// so the writer must commit files named in ExecutableNames as 100755.\npackage roles\n\nimport \"embed\"\n\n// FS is the starter .ard/ tree `ard init` proposes: config.yaml plus the role\n// directories (scanners/cve, scanners/docs, scanners/error-codes, scanners/lint, scanners/trufflehog, triage/lead, triage/engineer, triage/product-manager, triage/architect, triage/designer, triage/documentation-planner, workers/engineer, reviewers/eng-review, reviewers/license-review, reviewers/product-manager-review and reviewers/security-review); paths are relative to .ard/.\n//\n// scanners/missing-tests is left out until its scan driver exists; re-add it when wiring it in.\n//\n//go:embed config.yaml reviewers scanners/cve scanners/docs scanners/error-codes scanners/lint scanners/trufflehog triage workers\nvar FS embed.FS\n\n// ExecutableNames lists base names that must be written 0755.\nvar ExecutableNames = []string{\"scan\"}\ninternal/roles/config.yaml:42:  scanners/trufflehog: { every: 24h, max_open: 5, group_size: 1, autoclose: true, route: needs-human, timeout: 30m }\ninternal/initcmd/body.go:39:\tb.WriteString(\"- `scanners/trufflehog` is included. It files leaked-credential issues for a human (never for an agent) and needs a TruffleHog binary (AGPL-3.0; it is installed by the role's Dockerfile or taken from the host, and is not in the ard image). To opt out, delete `.ard/scanners/trufflehog/` and its `scanners/trufflehog` line under `overrides:` in `.ard/config.yaml` before merging.\\n\")\ndocs/TODO.md:22:- #203 Scanner: trufflehog (leaked secrets, human-routed)\ndocs/TODO.md:25:- #216 Scanner: trufflehog role (#203 part 2)\ndocs/TODO.md:26:- #217 Scanner: trufflehog starter wiring and image pin (#203 part 3)\ndocs/TODO.md:47:- #224 Scanner: trufflehog history scan\ndocs/layout.md:27:internal/roles/             starter .ard/ tree (config.yaml, role dirs) embedded for ard init (scanners/cve, scanners/docs, scanners/error-codes, scanners/lint, scanners/trufflehog, triage/lead, triage/engineer, workers/engineer, reviewers/eng-review, reviewers/license-review, reviewers/security-review)\ndocs/proposal.md:214:| trufflehog | leaked-credential scan of the current commit (`sh` + `jq` + TruffleHog) | 24 h | 1 | yes |\ndocs/proposal.md:227:**The trufflehog scanner** (`scanners/trufflehog`, a `sh` script plus one `jq` program) runs `trufflehog filesystem . --json --no-update --no-color --no-verification --no-ignore-tag --fail-on-scan-errors --concurrency=2` on the current commit. It never verifies a credential against a provider. Only the detector name, file, line and a hash of the secret leave the scan: `Raw`, `RawV2`, `Redacted`, `SecretParts`, `ExtraData` and `StructuredData` stay in pipes inside `scan`. The fingerprint is `trufflehog:` plus the first 16 hex digits of SHA-256 over `ard-trufflehog-v1`, a NUL byte and the base64 of the secret (an unsalted hash, so one value gives one issue wherever it appears). The scan fails closed: a non-zero trufflehog exit, a missing `finished scanning` summary, zero chunks on a non-empty tree, or a result count that differs from the summary produces no findings, so nothing is autoclosed on a partial run. `exclude-paths` (regexes; `.git` is always excluded) and `allow` (one fingerprint per line) are human-owned; a bad `allow` entry fails the run. Findings use `route: needs-human`, severity high, and carry a runbook that says to rotate the credential first. `commit` is the scanned SHA, recorded in `.ard/<n>/issue.md`; history is not scanned. TruffleHog is AGPL-3.0: it is installed by the role's Dockerfile and is not in the published `ard` image.\ndocs/proposal.md:432:  scanners/trufflehog:      { every: 24h, max_open: 5, group_size: 1, autoclose: true, route: needs-human, timeout: 30m }\ndocs/proposal.md:447:**`ard init` proposes the starter `.ard/` as a PR (decided, #27).** It builds `config.yaml` and the starter roles in memory (today `scanners/cve`, `scanners/docs`, `scanners/error-codes`, `scanners/lint`, `scanners/trufflehog`, `triage/lead`, `triage/engineer`, `workers/engineer`, `reviewers/eng-review`, `reviewers/license-review`, `reviewers/product-manager-review` and `reviewers/security-review`; `intake: {mode: label}`, the protected-path defaults above, and the cve, docs, error-codes, lint, lead, engineer, worker, eng-review, security-review, license-review and product-manager-review overrides), compares them with `main`, commits them on a new branch `ard-init` cut from `main` through the effect layer and a narrow committer lane, pushes it and opens a PR. It writes nothing to the local working tree or to `main`, and `scan` is committed `100755`. Files that already exist on `main` with different contents are a conflict naming the paths; `--force` proposes overwriting them, and init never deletes anything. It refuses while `ard-init` exists on the remote, whatever its PR's state, so it never force-pushes over or stacks commits on a human's edits: merge or close the PR, delete the branch and rerun. If `main` already has every starter file it prints `nothing to propose`. It syncs the label catalogue first (like `ard labels sync`), so a failure leaves nothing pushed. With `--dry-run` the commit, push and PR are logged to the ledger instead of acting. A missing r