{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-sonnet-5-5","id":"msg_011ChLhQR7kwnQcRrmuNxSj5","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"I added the `scanners/trufflehog-history` scanner and the executor change that lets scanner jobs read git history. `go test ./...` passes, but I didn't run `make lint` and the Docker integration test isn't written. `gofmt -l` flags only `internal/roles/testdata/docs/skips/src/_x.go`, an existing fixture that doesn't parse.\n\n- **Executor:** a new `Job.History` field is allowed only for scanner jobs. Docker mounts the controller's bare clone at `/history:ro` and sets `ARD_HISTORY`; host mode points at the clone path.\n- **How a scanner asks for it:** a role gets history when its directory holds an empty file named `history` (`Role.ReadsHistory()`). There is no config key, so a config override can't grant it.\n- **Scanner:** it runs `trufflehog git` over every fetched ref, with the same hash salt as the HEAD scanner, so a value has the same fingerprint in both. Only detector, file, line and the hash leave the scan. The commit, email and timestamp are dropped.\n- **Defaults:** runs every 7d, never autocloses, routes to needs-human, 60m timeout, max 5 open.\n- **Starter and docs:** the scanner is embedded in the starter tree and `ard init`'s PR body mentions it. `docs/proposal.md`, `docs/layout.md` and `docs/TODO.md` are updated.\n- **Starter sort fix:** `starter()` now sorts by full path. Without that, `trufflehog/` would list before `trufflehog-history/`.\n- **Tests:**\n  - validation, `Prepare` and docker argv;\n  - `ReadsHistory` and the engine job;\n  - the embedded role;\n  - a new `internal/roles/trufflehog_history_test.go` covering fingerprint parity, no leaked markers, failing closed, argv, missing tool or `ARD_HISTORY`, and the zero-chunks check.\n\nOpen points:\n- **Docker integration test:** the plan asked for one (git log inside a container, write to `/history` fails), and I didn't add it. I haven't tested the mount against real Docker, including whether the `safe.directory` setting is needed.\n- **Unmerged branches:** the read-only mount exposes every fetched ref, including unmerged PR branches. A maintainer should confirm the mount over a bundle.\n- **Enabling it here:** this repo needs a maintainer-made copy under `.ard/scanners/` and an entry in `.ard/config.yaml`, which I can't edit.\n- **Cross-scanner dedup:** whether a value found by both scanners becomes one issue depends on engine behaviour I didn't change.\n\nThe report is at `.ard/224/worker-engineer.md`."}],"container":null,"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":1163,"cache_read_input_tokens":71894,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":1163},"output_tokens":763,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"global","speed":"standard"},"input_transformations":[],"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"74408439-f49d-4817-a8b7-ff57f9f6ddad","uuid":"24d7b038-c938-48e1-91aa-5a541405ee32","timestamp":"2026-11-23T23:05:34.360Z","request_id":"req_011ChLhQQyL2WR5AywnX8ALA"}
